    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Looking at it through the lens of \"cultural and linguistic scaffolding,\" do you think there's a measurable difference in the actual mental processing or analytical rigor required to master these formal registers? In other words, is there an inherent correlation where students who rely more heavily on non-standard dialects might demonstrate less \"cognitive discipline\" in structured, logical argumentation compared to those raised in standard academic environments?",
